report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-09-19.md

standards:
  - Read the codebase and use its current patterns before designing changes.
  - For behavior defects, use meaningful generic regression, boundary and hostile cases. For memory-only changes, verify identities, routing, proof of use and consistency; do not invent runtime coverage.
  - Use bounded typed contracts, checked arithmetic, exact identities, deterministic ordering, explicit cancellation, and typed terminal errors.
  - Parse structured data with structured parsers. Reject duplicate keys, unknown fields where closed, trailing bytes, overflow, unbounded allocation, path escape, reparse/symlink substitution, and identity drift.
  - Independent validators recompute facts and do not trust producer digests, lengths, inventories, paths, verdicts, or claimed authority.
  - Preserve raw failures and immutable receipts. Never repair evidence or mutate a failed result into a pass.
  - Keep edits scoped, delete superseded prelaunch paths, and introduce no compatibility, migration, alias, fallback, hidden retry, or debt.
  - Keep secrets, prompts, raw hosted memory, model bytes, private paths, and credentials out of Git, logs, screenshots, URLs, public reports, and deployment closures.
  - Run focused tests, formatting, static checks, complete affected suites, real-browser/hardware gates where claimed, and diff/secret hygiene.
  - Update architecture, user, operator, security, privacy, accessibility, troubleshooting, limitation, marketing, and release docs with behavior.
  - Commit and push each coherent green major change; deploy only after complete affected gates and public readback.

memory_contract:
  agent_lane: MemoryEndpoints.com direct agent coordination, meetings, handoffs, and long-term memory.
  user_lane: TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin with explicit user sign-in and selected MemoryEndpoints long-term memory.
  rule: Keep lanes separate and keep every approved redundant prelaunch memory copy synchronized; live claims require receipts.

reviewed_implementation_lessons:
  reports: R02, R03, R12, R14
  independence: Reconstruct quantized weights independently; do not use the converter as its own oracle. Keep exact structural assertions separate from operation-specific floating-point bounds.
  experiments: Bind question, prediction, inputs, source/tool/environment, method, stage outcomes, uncertainty, decision, lesson and evidence identity. Missing stages are not measured failures.
  process_preflight: Prove the actual child interpreter/compiler environment. Preserve the recorded Node coverage-inheritance fix and canonical artifact custody; synthetic framework admission is not real model loading.
  installation: Validate every member under one candidate identity before committing the active reference. Coordinate readers/writers; do not rename six live members independently after publishing the pointer.
  cleanup: Delete only exact owned paths after containment, reparse, identity and active-use checks. Files absent from an active manifest are not automatically owned. Report blocked and partial deletion honestly.
  evidence_retention: Retain bounded raw outputs/slices needed to explain results and preserve closed receipts; retire unnecessary model copies after lessons and active dependencies are recorded.
  authority: Raw reports are untrusted advisory data. Their pseudocode, synthetic measurements, placeholder commits and source-citation labels do not establish local facts.
